  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">She Leads - Liberia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Girls and young women  (age 14 till 24) are the primary target group of the She Leads programme. Especially those that experience intersecting forms of discrimination and exclusion such as GYW living in poor, remot rural areas and urban slums, GYW experiencing GBV, GYW with different abilities, GYW who are out of school, GYW from sexual minority groups and refugees and internally displaced GYW. In addition, the programme works closely with CSO organisations and networks, (representatives of) formal institutions and community members and leaders.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In all She Leads countries, girls and young women, particularly GYW from socially excluded and exploited groups, are denied the opportunity to voice their interests and to participate meaningfully in decision-making processes. While many countries have made impressive strides in, for example, GYW&#x2019;s access to education and the introduction of new laws against GBV, their socio-political participation continues to be much lower than that of boys and young men. Within the population of girls and young women (between age 14 till 24 years of age), there are specific groups of GYW in She Leads countries who suffer most from (intersectional) discrimination and exclusion.She Leads is a joint programme of Plan International Netherlands, Defence for Children - ECPAT the Netherlands (DCI-ECPAT), African Women&#x2019;s Development and Communication Network (FEMNET), and Terre des Hommes the Netherlands (TdH). Equal Measures 2030 is a technical partner. The She Leads consortium brings together child rights organisations, feminist/women&#x2019;s rights organisations, and GYW-led groups and aims to increase sustained influence of girls and young women (GYW) on decision-making and the transformation of gender norms in formal and informal institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The She Leads programme will focus its interventions on: GYW living in poor, remote rural areas and urban slums, GYW experiencing gender based violence (particularly girls who have married early), GYW with disabilities, GYW who are out of school (including teenage mothers), Refugee and internally displaced GYW and GYW from sexual minority groups the above mentioned groups. The long-term aim (impact) of our programme is that GYW&#x2019;s perspectives are included in gender responsive laws and policies and societal norms and practices.</narrative>
  </description>
